      "source": [
        "### Analyze Class Distribution and Calculate Class Weights\n",
        "\n",
        "To address the class imbalance, we'll first analyze the distribution of samples across different classes in the training dataset. Then, we'll calculate class weights, which will be used during model training to give more importance to under-represented classes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "9b6f2eb5",
        "outputId": "dcb7f3f1-5cda-49e5-b167-27200b7e725c"
      },
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.utils import class_weight\n",
        "\n",
        "# Collect all labels from the training dataset to calculate class distribution\n",
        "# Note: This might be slow for very large datasets if not cached/prefetched effectively.\n",
        "print(\"Collecting labels from training dataset...\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Unbatch and then collect labels\n",
        "all_labels = []\n",
        "for _, labels_batch in train_ds.unbatch():\n",
        "    all_labels.append(labels_batch.numpy())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert to numpy array\n",
        "all_labels = np.array(all_labels)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Class distribution in training dataset:\")\n",
        "unique_labels, counts = np.unique(all_labels, return_counts=True)\n",
        "for label, count in zip(unique_labels, counts):\n",
        "    print(f\"  Class '{class_names[label]}': {count} samples\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate class weights\n",
        "# `compute_class_weight` expects `classes` (all possible class labels) and `y` (actual labels in dataset).\n",
        "class_weights = class_weight.compute_class_weight(\n",
        "    class_weight='balanced',\n",
        "    classes=np.arange(num_classes),\n",
        "    y=all_labels\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert to a dictionary for easy use with model.fit\n",
        "class_weight_dict = dict(enumerate(class_weights))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nCalculated Class Weights:\")\n",
        "for i, weight in class_weight_dict.items():\n",
        "    print(f\"  Class '{class_names[i]}': {weight:.2f}\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
