      "source": [
        "## Build the Model (Transfer Learning with EfficientNet)\n",
        "\n",
        "We will use transfer learning with a pre-trained EfficientNetB0 model. This approach leverages a model already trained on a large dataset (like ImageNet) and adapts it to our specific task. We'll add a few layers on top of the EfficientNet base to classify our brain MRI images."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 377
        },
        "id": "a220b1d4",
        "outputId": "a0ee090a-7f8d-4feb-cf60-7e48d845c06b"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Load the pre-trained EfficientNetB0 model from tf.keras.applications\n",
        "# We exclude the top (classification) layer, as we'll add our own.\n",
        "base_model = tf.keras.applications.EfficientNetB0(input_shape=(img_height, img_width, 3),\n",
        "                                                  include_top=False,\n",
        "                                                  weights='imagenet')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Freeze the base model to prevent its weights from being updated during training.\n",
        "# This preserves the learned features from ImageNet.\n",
        "base_model.trainable = False\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create a new model on top\n",
        "inputs = keras.Input(shape=(img_height, img_width, 3))\n",
        "x = base_model(inputs, training=False)\n",
        "x = keras.layers.GlobalAveragePooling2D()(x)\n",
        "x = keras.layers.Dropout(0.2)(x) # Add a dropout layer for regularization\n",
        "x = keras.layers.Dense(256, activation='relu')(x) # Additional dense layer\n",
        "x = keras.layers.Dropout(0.3)(x) # Another dropout layer\n",
        "outputs = keras.layers.Dense(num_classes, activation='softmax')(x)\n",
        "model = keras.Model(inputs, outputs)\n",
        "\n",
        "model.summary()\n"
      ],
